{"version":1,"slug":"Oliiveboardd__Quant_Super_Prac__SSC_Super_Practice_LCM_and_HCF_4","path":"Oliiveboardd/Quant Super Prac/SSC_Super_Practice_LCM_and_HCF_4.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Oliiveboardd","category":"Quant Super Prac","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If A, B, and C are coprime numbers then which of the following is true?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2360;&#2361;&#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">HCF of (A, BC) = A</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(A, BC) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) = A</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">HCF of (A, BC) = 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(A, BC) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) = 1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">HCF of (B, AC) = A</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(B, AC) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) = A</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">HCF of (B, AC) = B</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(B, AC) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) = B</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let A = 3, B = 5, and C = 7,</p><p>Now HCF of (A, BC) = HCF of (3, 35) = 1</p><p>HCF of (B, AC) = HCF of (5, 21) = 1</p><p>Hence option b is true.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Let the HCF of X and Y be 'M' and let Y = MN. LCM of X and Y is given by:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 'M' &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Y = MN &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">XN</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">XN</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">MN</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">MN</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">YN</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">YN</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">XY</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">XY</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>We know that,</p><p>HCF * LCM = product of numbers</p><p>M * LCM = X * Y</p><p>LCM = X * MN/M</p><p>LCM = XN</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the H.C.F. of 95, 380, 665?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>95, 380, 665 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">95</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">95</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">78</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">78</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">190</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">190</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>95, 380, 665</p><p></p><p>95 = 19 x 5</p><p>380 = 19 x 5 x 4</p><p>665 = 19 x 7 x 5</p><p></p><p>Therefore, the H.C.F is 19 x 5 = 95</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The least number which is exactly divisible by 3, 8, 5, 12, and 4. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 3, 8, 5, 12 &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;&#2307; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>L.C.M of 3, 8, 5, 12, and 4 = 120</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the LCM of 48, 56, and 72?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>48, 56 &#2324;&#2352; 72 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1014</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1014</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1012</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1012</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1010</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1010</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1008</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1008</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Multiple of 48 = 2 * 2 * 2 * 2 * 3</p><p>Multiple of 56 = 2 * 2 * 2 * 7</p><p>Multiple of 72 = 2 * 2 * 2 * 3 * 3</p><p>LCM of 48 , 56 and 72 = 2 * 2 * 2 * 3 * 2 * 7 * 3 = 1008</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p><div>&nbsp;What is the Least Common Multiple <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>8</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>7</span></div> , <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>9</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>14</span></div> , and <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>16</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>7</span></div> &quest;&nbsp;</div></p><p></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;-</p><p><div><div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>8</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>7</span></div> , <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>9</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>14</span></div> , and <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>16</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>7</span></div></div></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">144/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144/7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72/7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">288/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">288/7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48/7</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Least Common Multiple 8/7, 9/14, and 16/7 = (LCM of 8, 9, and 16)/(HCF of 7, 14) = 144/7</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The product of the smallest common multiple and the biggest common factor of 45, 90, 120, and 150 is: </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>45, 90, 120 &#2324;&#2352; 150 &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2700</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2700</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Smallest common multiple (L.C.M) of 45, 90, 120, and 150 = 1800 </p><p>Biggest common factor (H.C.F) of 45, 90, 120, and 150 = 15 </p><p>Hence, the product of L.C.M and H.C.F = 1800 * 15 = 27000 </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If LCM and HCF of two numbers is 576 and 8 respectively and their sum is 136. Find the smallest number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 576 &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 136 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">56</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">56</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let numbers are '8a' and '8b' (a and b are co-prime and a &gt; b).</p><p>LCM of 8a and 8b = 8ab = 576</p><p>ab = 72 .... (1)</p><p>Sum = 8a + 8b = 136</p><p>(a + b) = 17 .... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>a = 9 and b = 8</p><p>Smallest number = 8b = 64</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The least number which when divided by 18, 12, 16 and 24 leaves remainder 6 in each case is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 18, 12, 16 &#2324;&#2352; 24 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 6 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376; :</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">132</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">132</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">156</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">156</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Least number which when divided by 18, 12, 16 and 24 leaves remainder 6 in each case = LCM of 18, 12, 16 and 24 + Common remainder</p><p>LCM of 18, 12, 16 and 24 = 144</p><p>Common remainder = 6</p><p>Required number = 144 + 6</p><p>= 150</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ratio of LCM of two numbers to the HCF of same numbers is 42: 1. The difference between the LCM and HCF is 738. If one number is 108, then what is the other number?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 42: 1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 738 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 108 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">84</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">84</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">126</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">126</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">112</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>LCM/HCF = 42/1</p><p>=&gt; LCM = 42 * HCF</p><p>LCM - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; 42HCF - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 738/41</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 18</p><p>One number * another number = HCF * LCM</p><p>=&gt; 108 * another number = 18 * 42 * 18</p><p>=&gt; another number = 18 * 42 * 18/108</p><p>=&gt; another number = 126</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the ratio of numbers is 11: 8 and their H.C.F is 18, then find their L.C.M. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11:8 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (H.C.F) 18 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (L.C.M) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">891</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">891</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1188</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1188</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1584</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1584</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">792</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">792</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>L.C.M = Ratio value of 1<sup>st</sup> * ratio value of 2<sup>nd</sup> number * H.C.F </p><p>= 11 * 8 * 18 </p><p>= 1584 </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The Highest common factor of 5/12, 7/24, 11/36, and 3/16 is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>5/12, 7/24, 11/36 &#2324;&#2352; 3/16 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1/144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/72</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1155/144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1155/144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1155/4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1155/4</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>H.C.F of fractions = (H.C.F of numerator)/ (L.C.M of denominator) </p><p>H.C.F of 5, 7, 11, and 3 = 1 </p><p>L.C.M of 12, 24, 36, and 16 = 144 </p><p>Hence, the required H.C.F = 1/144 </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the LCM of a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup> and c<sup>3</sup>+d<sup>3</sup>, where a= 5, b= 4, c=10 and d=2.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup> &#2324;&#2352; c<sup>3</sup>+d<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; a= 5, b= 4, c=10 &#2324;&#2352; d=2 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">190512</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">190512</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3024</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3024</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27216</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27216</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7056</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7056</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>According to the Question,</p><p>LCM of a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup> and c<sup>3</sup>+d<sup>3 </sup></p><p>Given that: a= 5, b= 4, c=10 and d=2</p><p>a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3 </sup>= 5<sup>3</sup>+4<sup>3 </sup>= 125 + 64 = 189</p><p>c<sup>3</sup>+d<sup>3 </sup>= 10<sup>3</sup>+2<sup>3 </sup>= 1000 + 8 = 1008</p><p>Now, LCM of 189 and 1008 is to be determined</p><p>Factors of 189 = 3 x 3 x 3 x 7</p><p>Factors of 1008 = 2x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3 x 7</p><p>So, LCM = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 3 x 3 x 3 x 7= 3024</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The ratio of the LCM of two numbers to the sum of the same two numbers is 12:7, if their HCF is 4, what is the product of these two numbers?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 12:7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">192</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">192</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">172</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">172</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">196</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">196</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">169</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">169</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>As the HCF of numbers is 4, let the numbers be 4y and 4z.</p><p>LCM of given two numbers = 4yz</p><p>As per given condition:</p><p>(4yz)/(4y+4z) = 12/7</p><p>yz/(y+z) = 12/7</p><p>yz = 12 and y+z = 7</p><p>For the above condition,</p><p>y = 4 and z = 3</p><p>Numbers = 4  X  4 = 16 and 3  X  4 = 12</p><p>Product of numbers = 16  X  12 = 192</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the ratio of two numbers is 3: 1 and their LCM is 126, then the sum of the two numbers is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:1 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; 126 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">172</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">172</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">168</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">168</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">196</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">196</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">184</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">184</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers are 3X and X.</p><p>LCM of 3X and X = 3X</p><p>Given,</p><p>3X = 126</p><p>X = 42</p><p>Sum of numbers = 3X + X = 4X = 4 * 42 = 168</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the LCM of U and 12 is 156 and the HCF of U and 15 is 1, find the sum of the digits of U.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; U &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) 156 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; U &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 1 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; U &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>LCM of U and 12 is 156 and the HCF of U and 15 is 1</p><p>So, U = 13</p><p>sum of the digits of U = 1 + 3 = 4</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>LCM and HCF of three numbers 28, 36, and 48 are x and y, respectively, then x is how many times of y?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; 28, 36 &#2324;&#2352; 48 &#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; x, y &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">252</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">252</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">126</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">126</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">378</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">378</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">63</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">63</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>LCM of 28, 36, 48 = x = 1008</p><p>HCF of 28, 36, 48 = y = 4</p><p>So, x/y = 1008/4 = 252</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If LCM and HCF of two numbers are 819 and 13 respectively and one number is 91, then what is the other number?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 819 &#2324;&#2352; 13 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 91 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">104</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">104</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">117</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">117</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">143</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">143</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">156</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">156</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>One number * another number = LCM * HCF</p><p>=&gt; 91 * another number = 819 * 13</p><p>=&gt; another number = 819 * 13/91</p><p>=&gt; another number = 117</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Three numbers are in the ratio of 12: 7: 15 and their HCF is 9. What is the sum of these numbers?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 12:7:15 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">316</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">316</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">216</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">216</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">306</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">306</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">206</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">206</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Sum of ratios = 12 + 7 + 15 = 34</p><p>Sum of these numbers = 34 x 9 = 306</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The HCF of two numbers is 25 and their LCM is 4250. If one number is 70% more than the other number, then find the larger number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 25 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) 4250 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 70% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">525</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">525</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">375</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">375</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">425</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">425</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">600</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers be 100a and 170a.</p><p>Now,</p><p>100a*170a = 25*4250</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 6.25</p><p>a = 2.5</p><p>So, larger number = 170*2.5 = 425</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}